public static String formatTimeDate(int one, int two, int three, Boolean isDate) 
{
    String s;
    if (isDate) {
        s = one + "/" + two + "/" + three;
    } 
    else {
        s = one + ":" + two + ":" + three;
    }
    return s;
}
Control ﬂags may also indicate low cohesion – where a method/function performs more 
than one distinct task.
formatTimeDate() formats dates, and formats times.
These tasks are similar, but not really a single responsibility.
